      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This sense of value tied to one's usefulness is a classic conundrum, especially in an era of rapid technological advancements. It's as if you're measuring your worth by the metric of your relevance to the new systems, rather than your inherent value as a person. This can lead to feelings of self-doubt and questioning your purpose, leaving you wondering if you're indeed just an inefficiency. It's essential to recognize that you have more to offer than just skills or abilities.",
